# PIN-HOLD — the catalogue is deliberately behind upstream. Do not "catch it up".
#
# Read by scripts/verify-application-pin.sh --drift, which downgrades its alarm to a
# notice while this file names the currently-pinned tag. Delete the file when the hold
# ends; a hold naming a tag that is no longer pinned is reported as stale and loud.
#
# This exists because BEHIND is a true reading of a deliberate state, and the agent that
# reads it may be a fresh session after a restart with none of this context. A held pin
# that is only held in someone's head gets pinned away by the next person doing the
# obviously-right thing.
#
# 2026-09-13, UPDATED: the original reason was "imac is mid stage-4 install". Stage 4 has
# since PASSED (urb-agents #807), so that reason expired within hours of being written.
# The hold stands for a different reason, below. Recording the update rather than editing
# silently, because a hold whose stated reason has quietly expired is the exact failure
# this file was built to catch — and it caught its own.

held_tag: v20260913-7deb4a2
newer_upstream: v20260913-eba547e
since: 2026-09-13
refs: urb-agents #803, #804

reason: >-
  atlas published eba547e and explicitly declined to ask for a pin: "I would rather it
  waited for a reason to move than move for tidiness — pinning is where stage 2 restarts,
  and nothing in this build changes behaviour." ops-dev's position after stage 4 passed:
  it "rides whenever something real next moves". So the hold is no longer about protecting
  a running verification — that finished — it is that a pin costs a stage-2 round and this
  build has not earned one.

release_when: >-
  When something real next moves — a behaviour change worth a stage-2 round — and eba547e
  (or its successor) is nominated. NOT on tidiness, and not merely because drift reports
  behind.

carry_forward: >-
  Two things to apply when eba547e IS pinned, both easy to lose between now and then.

  1. PASS CONDITION: _warn_unrendered_operational must print NOTHING at install. atlas
     predicts every operational key is now in a rendered set, and nobody can verify that
     until it is installed. It depends on tor-agent's 1.6.68 rendering sets as much as on
     atlas's keys, so a silent warning is two systems agreeing rather than one being
     right.

  2. The code-location IMAGE digest WILL differ from 7deb4a2's, and that does not mean
     the tree changed. eba547e is text-only. The check is hashing the trees inside both
     images, not comparing image digests — confirmed twice now (imac on cfd2ca7/7deb4a2,
     and this repo on bfda7b6 from the other direction).
